(a) When used. Subsections (b) through (f) of this section contain generally acceptable compliance alternatives which may be approved by enforcement authorities in the city. The alternatives are incorporated in this article for the purpose of illustrating principles which can be applied to the solution of code noncompliance problems and are not necessarily acceptable under all circumstances. It is recognized for purposes of this article that all building systems interact with each other; therefore, any consideration of compliance alternatives must take into account all existing and proposed conditions to determine their acceptability. The principles applied may be used for the solution of similar compliance problems in other buildings and occupancy classifications. The compliance alternatives are not all-inclusive and do not preclude consideration and approval of other alternatives by an enforcement authority.
